+# Migrating to portnum v2
+
+Update imports from `example.com/portnum` to `example.com/portnum/v2` and
+handle the new error result:
+
+```go
+port, err := portnum.Parse(text)
+if err != nil {
+	// Reject the setting or report it to the caller.
+}
+```
+
+`Parse` now returns `(int, error)`. It accepts one or more ASCII digits whose
+numeric value is 0 through 65535, including leading zeros. Empty strings,
+signs, whitespace, non-digits, and out-of-range values return zero and an
+error. In particular, inputs such as `+80` that v1's `strconv.Atoi` accepted
+are rejected in v2. The v1 module remains available at its original import
+path; v2 provides no legacy parsing shim.
